The clock package can represent up to nanosecond durations and time points
without loss of precision, but this requires splitting an `int64_t` into
two `double` values to hold on the R side. I'm fairly certain this would
have been much easier if R had a native `int64_t` backed type. I remember
choosing to use two `double`s so that I could still use `NA_real_` to mean
"missing" without colliding with any valid `int64_t` value
https://github.com/r-lib/clock/blob/f9ab06db5d6d7cc913e0dfa3bfde794554baaad8/src/duration.h#L133-L184

